🤖 **Comment from Claude working with Aaron Silverman:**

**[P3]** Bind the IDs as one array, as `loadApplicableHoldouts` in this file does.

`id IN ?` binds one parameter per experiment ID. The holdout query below uses `a.id = ANY(?::uuid[])` with `pq.Array`.

<details>
<summary><b>Suggested patch</b> — the database-backed <code>TestRolloutState*</code> tests pass</summary>

```diff
--- a/domains/ffe/libs/flagging/core/repository/ufc_repository.go
+++ b/domains/ffe/libs/flagging/core/repository/ufc_repository.go
@@ -505,7 +505,7 @@ func loadExperimentRolloutState(tx *gorm.DB, orgID int64, flags []*model.Feature
 		return nil
 	}
 	var experiments []experimentModel.Experiment
-	if err := tx.Select("id", "state").Where("org_id = ? AND id IN ?", orgID, experimentIDs).Find(&experiments).Error; err != nil {
